# Finding Products

The Codexeron Marketplace provides tools to help buyers discover digital products that match their needs.

This guide explains how to search, compare, and evaluate products before purchasing.

---

# Searching Products

Buyers can search the marketplace using:

- Product names
- Keywords
- Categories
- Tags
- Technologies
- Features

Use specific search terms to find more relevant results.

---

# Categories

Products are organized into categories to make discovery easier.

Categories may include:

- PHP Applications
- Scripts
- Plugins
- APIs
- Libraries
- Themes
- Tools
- Other Digital Products

Available categories may expand as the marketplace grows.

---

# Product Information

Before purchasing a product, review the available information carefully.

Important details include:

- Product description
- Features
- Screenshots
- Demo information
- Requirements
- Supported technologies
- Version information
- Documentation
- License type

---

# Compatibility Check

Before buying a product, verify that it matches your requirements.

Check:

- Programming language
- Framework compatibility
- Database requirements
- Server requirements
- Required extensions

A compatibility check helps prevent problems after purchase.

---

# Comparing Products

When comparing products, consider:

- Features
- Product quality
- Documentation
- Update history
- Seller reputation
- Customer feedback

Choose the product that best fits your project requirements.

---

# Seller Information

Seller profiles can help buyers understand:

- Seller experience
- Published products
- Product activity
- Available support options

Seller information can be useful when making purchasing decisions.

---

# Product Reviews

Reviews and ratings can provide additional insight.

Consider:

- Customer experiences
- Product quality feedback
- Support responsiveness

Reviews should be evaluated together with the complete product information.

---

# Best Practices

Before purchasing:

- Read the complete description.
- Check compatibility.
- Review screenshots.
- Read documentation.
- Understand license terms.

Making an informed decision creates a better experience for both buyers and sellers.

